lg.l:
Oh! I beg your pardon, Signor.—I had really quite forgot, that you
                                were blind!—I am a thoughtless little fellow, Signor, without wit;
                                and, I am sorry to say, without money.—But I mean no harm, Signor;
                                and so I'll sing you a stanza:—and if you do not like it, I'll never
                                sing you another:—so you will only lose three minutes of time.
